# Line endings, and the one place they are not cosmetic.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and deployed to Linux. Git's autocrlf turns
# checked-out files into CRLF here, which is harmless for TypeScript — and fatal
# for anything the kernel executes: `#!/bin/sh\r` is not a shebang, and the
# error a Linux box gives back is the unhelpful "no such file or directory"
# pointing at an interpreter that plainly exists.
#
# infra/watchdog.sh is scp'd straight from a working copy to /usr/local/bin, so
# it must stay LF on disk, not only in the object store. The Dockerfiles and
# compose files are here for the same reason: they are read by Linux tooling,
# and a stray CR inside a RUN line has bitten this project before.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
